  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "ec816f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 0,
      "content": "CSUF General Transfer Information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5f836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements &amp; Admissions deadlines See approved General Education courses at CSU Fullerton. See Associate Degree for Transfer. See the Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP) .",
      "contentHtml": "<blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the Admissions website for </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/prospectivestudent/transferlocaladmissionarea.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">transfer admission requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> &amp; </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/deadlines/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Admissions deadlines</a></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.fullerton.edu/undergraduate/general-education/approved-courses.html#box5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">approved General Education </a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">courses at CSU Fullerton. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/associate-degree-for-transfer-major-and-campus-search.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Associate Degree for Transfer.</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/external-exams/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP)</a><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/student-services/casper/Pages/external-exam-credit.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">.</a></blockquote>"
    },
    {
      "id": "ee816f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About This Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "f4816f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The Bachelor of Arts in Religious Studies requires a minimum of 120 units, which includes 27 units in the major, General Education, all-university requirements, and free electives. Each course counted toward the major must be completed with a grade of \"C\"(2.0) or higher. Introduction and Methods (6 units) Religious Traditions 1: Judaism, Christianity, Islam (9 units) Religious Traditions 2: Hinduism, Buddhism, Jainisim, Sikhism (9 units) Religion, Culture and Experience (3 units) Writing Requirement: The course requirement of the university upper-division baccalaureate writing course is met through ENGL 301. It is highly recommended that students majoring in Religious Studies pursue the study of classical languages such as Arabic, Greek, Hebrew, Latin and Sanskrit when such languages are offered.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>The Bachelor of Arts in Religious Studies requires a minimum of 120 units, which includes 27 units in the major, General Education, all-university requirements, and free electives. Each course counted toward the major must be completed with a grade of \"C\"(2.0) or higher.</p><p><br></p><p>Introduction and Methods (6 units)</p><p>Religious Traditions 1: Judaism, Christianity, Islam (9 units)</p><p>Religious Traditions 2: Hinduism, Buddhism, Jainisim, Sikhism (9 units)</p><p>Religion, Culture and Experience (3 units)</p><p>Writing Requirement: The course requirement of the university upper-division baccalaureate writing course is met through ENGL 301.</p><p><br></p><p>It is highly recommended that students majoring in Religious Studies pursue the study of classical languages such as Arabic, Greek, Hebrew, Latin and Sanskrit when such languages are offered.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0816f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "(120 UNITS) The Bachelor of Arts in Religious Studies ( Link ) is for those who: want a humanities undergraduate background focusing on religion as a preparation for further study in such fields as education, law, politics, social work, counseling and government service; wish to pursue graduate studies in religion with the aim of teaching and/or conducting research in the subject; are considering a career in various religious ministries or in religious education. The curriculum provides new ways of understanding the world, exciting methods of analysis and sophistication in the interpretation of religious texts, beliefs and practices. Interacting with each other and outside communities, students learn to think, write and speak with clarity and precision, conduct research on complex issues and listen and relate to others with understanding and respect. In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree section in this catalog for complete information. Students must earn a “C” (2.0) or better in all courses applied toward the degree.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>(120 UNITS)</strong></p><p>The Bachelor of Arts in Religious Studies (<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=101&amp;poid=47260&amp;returnto=15150\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>) is for those who: want a humanities undergraduate background focusing on religion as a preparation for further study in such fields as education, law, politics, social work, counseling and government service; wish to pursue graduate studies in religion with the aim of teaching and/or conducting research in the subject; are considering a career in various religious ministries or in religious education. The curriculum provides new ways of understanding the world, exciting methods of analysis and sophistication in the interpretation of religious texts, beliefs and practices. Interacting with each other and outside communities, students learn to think, write and speak with clarity and precision, conduct research on complex issues and listen and relate to others with understanding and respect.</p><p><br></p><p>In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/content.php?catoid=101&amp;navoid=15099\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree</a>&nbsp;section in this catalog for complete information.&nbsp;Students must earn a “C” (2.0) or better in all courses applied toward the degree.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2816f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "Transfer Success Pathway major eligible",
      "contentHtml": "<p><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/transfer-success-pathway.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Success Pathway</a> major eligible </p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "b8a730af-af06-4545-b0d0-019d68d6b5af",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 6,
      "content": "The information provided here is subject to change without notice. Please be advised that articulation agreements published here may be updated or added at any time. Be sure to check with a counselor or adviser for the most current requirements. For additional transfer information: For C-ID information: https://c-idsystem.org/courses/ For Common Course Numbering: https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/",
      "contentHtml": "<p></p><p></p><p><strong><em>The&nbsp;information&nbsp;provided&nbsp;here&nbsp;is&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;change&nbsp;without&nbsp;notice.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;be&nbsp;advised&nbsp;that&nbsp;articulation&nbsp;agreements&nbsp;published&nbsp;here&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;updated&nbsp;or&nbsp;added&nbsp;at&nbsp;any&nbsp;time.&nbsp;Be&nbsp;sure&nbsp;to&nbsp;check&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;counselor&nbsp;or&nbsp;adviser&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;current&nbsp;requirements.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>For&nbsp;additional&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;information:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>For&nbsp;C-ID&nbsp;information:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://c-idsystem.org/courses/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://c-idsystem.org/courses/</a></li><li>For&nbsp;Common&nbsp;Course&nbsp;Numbering:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/</a></li></ul>"
    }
